<title>DENMARK: Danish June North Sea oil production up 31.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Danish June North Sea oil production up 31.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish Underground Consortium (DUC) oil production from its North Sea fields rose 31.3 percent in June 1997 from June 1996, operator A.P. Moeller Group said on Monday.</p>
<p>A spokesman said oil production was 936,000 tonnes in June, or 229,303 barrels per day (bpd), compared with 174,706 bpd in June, 1996.</p>
<p>DUC is responsible for virtually the entire output from Denmark's North Sea oil and gas fields.</p>
</text>
